  "headline": "Indonesian Provinces Announce New Provincial Minimum Wage For 2027",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesia 2027 Minimum Wage Policy",
  "metaDescription": "Indonesian provincial governments have announced 2027 minimum wage figures following a government-mandated deadline for formalizing the new pay rates.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Provincial governments across Indonesia are announcing 2027 minimum wage figures by the government's November 21 deadline.",
    "West Java, Yogyakarta, and South Sulawesi have disclosed their updated wage rates as part of the nationwide policy rollout.",
    "The Ministry of Manpower has stated that new wage formulas incorporate cost of living standards and local economic conditions."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government issued a directive requiring all regional leaders to finalize and announce Provincial Minimum Wage (UMP) figures by November 21, 2026, followed by district-level minimum wage (UMK) determinations on November 25. Central government officials, including the Minister of Manpower and the Minister of Home Affairs, instructed regional administrations to strictly oversee this process. Regional governments have begun releasing their specific 2027 wage rates, such as West Java setting the figure at Rp3 million, the Yogyakarta Special Region at Rp2.7 million, and South Sulawesi at approximately Rp4.23 million. The Ministry of Manpower emphasized that the calculation process involves assessing the Decent Living Needs (KHL) index and overall regional economic stability. Business associations have urged authorities to consider current company operational conditions during the deliberation, while labor unions have advocated for the KHL to remain a primary benchmark in wage calculations.",
